 "discoveries": [
  "DISCOVERY: (claim, exhaustive C enumeration of all basic sparse solutions + Held-Karp) in every 5-variable walk cube from {e, v, u, pe, q1, y0..y3, six corner-pair flags, A} with null dimension <= 12 and frame <= 61 CX, every 12-term Walsh support gives frame + shortest free-end tour >= 73 CX (F1 cube (e, pe, a, y1, y3): exactly 8 such supports, tours 17-18 paid toggles; seed cube (e, q1, a, y1, y3): tour 15 on a 58-CX frame), so a 12-rotation walk at 71 CX needs a 6th walk variable.",
  "DISCOVERY: (claim) replacing the ladder CX(f3 -> f1) by CX(f0 -> f1) costs nothing and makes all three ladder CX pivot-controlled, so the free-end rule extends to all of span{u, v, e}; with u, v, e and the w slots every nonzero form of span{u, v, e} is a 1-CX toggle, i.e. the bright layer is a complete graph K8 for the walk."
 ],
